  <prompt>
    Author the `compose-summarize-word-changes` capability as an Action row + Click-path Binding row (ADR-039), mirror-first under infra/dataverse/, dispatched through the shipped session-dispatch seam (NO new endpoint). The Action produces a human-friendly summary of what changed in a returned-from-Word DOCX version and returns `{summary, changes: [{kind: "insertion"|"deletion"|"comment"|"structural", location, description}]}` (FR-10). It is invoked by the return-from-Word flow (design §2.5) and consumes the `compose-document` JPS scope. Ships with eval cases in task 045.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    AI platform developer fluent in JPS Action authoring, the ADR-039 Action+Binding catalog model, the Word round-trip (DOCX pull / re-anchor) flow, and OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator constraints.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A deployable `compose-summarize-word-changes` Action row (change-summary SystemPrompt + OutputSchemaJson + Temperature + ModelDeploymentId) and its Click-path Binding row, authored mirror-first through the core's hoisted description source, consuming `compose-document`, invoked by the return-from-Word flow, returning schema `{summary: string, changes: [{kind: "insertion"|"deletion"|"comment"|"structural", location, description}]}` passing OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator with no property-level boolean `required`. Zero new routes; eval-ready for task 045.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Spec FR-10 + design §2.5 (Return from Word) + §7 (Catalog Roster row 5). A read/summarize action invoked automatically after a Word round-trip (FR-25 pull + FR-27 re-anchor produce the changed-version input): the LLM turns the structured change set into a human-friendly narrative. Consumes the R1 `compose-document` scope (enriched by the FR-22 semantic appendix). No `compose` disposition. Depends on Spike 6 (reverse round-trip) landing the return-from-Word input shape.
    </background>
